The task: add local request recording （请求记录） to contractlab:

- Records only in-process memory, no files.
- Admin scope: `/__contractlab` itself and `/__contractlab/` prefix — all requests there are NOT recorded and don't consume sequences. Note: currently the admin handling is only for exact HEALTH_PATH and RELOAD_PATH; other paths under the prefix fall through to business matching (which would 404 since config can't define them). The requirement says admin scope = `/__contractlab` itself and `/__contractlab/` prefix; all requests in that scope are not recorded and don't consume business sequences. Currently a request to `/__contractlab/foo` would fall to business matching → 404, and wouldn't consume sequence anyway (no endpoint can match since config rejects those paths). But with recording, we must make sure those 404s are NOT recorded. So the dispatch should check admin scope first: if pathname === '/__contractlab' or starts with '/__contractlab/', handle admin routes (health, reload, records query, records clear), else 404 without recording.

- For each request outside admin scope that is fully received and within body limit: record once — covering scenario responses, 400 body rejections, and unmatched 404s. Aborted or too-large: no record, no sequence consumption (already the case).

- Assign process-unique increasing IDs in order of completed reception; IDs separate from sequence consumption positions; never reused after clear or reload.

- Record must reconstruct: method, raw request target including query string, received request headers, raw body bytes; invalid UTF-8 must be losslessly represented with encoding noted — not replaced by parsed JSON. So store body as base64 plus maybe utf8 text when valid. E.g. `body: { encoding: 'utf-8', text: '...' }` or `{ encoding: 'base64', base64: '...' }`.

- Record config version selected at complete-reception time, match & body-validation results; 400 keeps the actual diff report returned.

- Qualified requests record reserved response item position; each record includes status, application-layer response headers, and body of the scenario or framework planned response, including accurate version header. Query string still not in matching; last-item reuse records same position; rejections and 404 have no consumption position.

- During delay, request is queryable with "pending" （待发送） status; after server finishes writing → "sent"; if connection drops before write completes or send fails → "interrupted". Sent only means server finished writing, not that client received; after sent, normal connection close doesn't change to interrupted. Disconnect after reservation still counts as consumed.

- Reload (success or failure) preserves records; in-flight requests keep their version/validation/planned response; later requests use version at their own reception-complete time. Query returns consistent snapshot at call time, doesn't advance sequences. Clear removes all records at that time including pending ones, but doesn't cancel responses, change config/version/sequences; requests fully received before clear that complete/fail afterwards must NOT reappear; requests fully received after clear are recorded normally.

So the clear semantics: clear sets a generation/cutoff — records whose id <= maxIdAtClear are dropped and their later status updates must not recreate them. Implementation: keep a Map<id, record>; clear() replaces the map with a new empty one. Status updates for in-flight requests mutate the record object directly (they hold a reference), so after clear the old record object is orphaned — updates to it don't reappear in the new map. That satisfies "不得重新出现" naturally.

ID counter: monotonically increasing, module-level, never reset.

